  {{!-- ogl (the WebGL library behind every gradflow canvas) is fetched from
        unpkg by gradflow-background.js's dynamic import('ogl'), resolved via
        the importmap at the top of this file. That import is the real floor
        on how fast any gradflow background can paint: the canvas cannot draw
        its first frame until the module has arrived, which on a fresh load
        means a cold connection (DNS + TLS + fetch) before anything happens.
        preconnect warms the connection in parallel with the rest of <head>;
        modulepreload fetches the module itself at high priority so the
        dynamic import() later resolves from cache instead of starting the
        round trip then. Directly shortens the "page background visible,
        gradflow not yet" window on a post→close return. --}}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://unpkg.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="modulepreload" href="https://unpkg.com/ogl@1.0.11/src/index.js" crossorigin>
