  {{!-- LOAD SCRIM — homepage only, and the first element in <body>.

        {{#is "index"}} is load-bearing, not tidiness. The scrim is only
        ever revealed by preloader.js, and #preloader is rendered by
        index.hbs alone ({{> preloader}}) — so on any other template this
        markup is an opaque, z-index:999998, full-viewport layer with
        nothing that will ever take it away. Rendered unguarded it covered
        /about/ completely for a full 6 SECONDS until particle-morph.hbs's
        unrelated 6s failsafe happened to clear it (measured: opacity 1 /
        transform 0 at 4s, cleared by 7s). Post pages escaped only because
        their own particle path clears it earlier. Keep this guard in sync
        with index.hbs's {{> preloader}} — the two must appear on exactly
        the same set of pages.

        Two hard requirements drove the PLACEMENT (first in <body>):

        1. STACKING. It was originally nested inside #particle-morph-demo
           (particle-morph.hbs), which is position:fixed + z-index:1 and so
           forms a stacking context — its own z-index:999998 was capped at
           the parent's level of 1 and it painted BELOW .hero (z-index:2).
           It never actually covered the hero at all. At body level it
           competes in the root stacking context, where that z-index means
           what it says.

        2. TIMING. particle-morph.hbs is included near the END of <body>
           (~line 1934), after ~96 blocking <script> tags including three.js
           and GSAP from external CDNs. The scrim therefore did not exist
           until DOMContentLoaded was almost due, which is what forced
           preloader.js to wait for that event before it could reveal the
           scrim — traced: the preloader's own fade-in finished at 2404ms
           but the scrim could not be touched until 3959ms, leaving the text
           sitting fully visible for ~1.5s of dead time. Declared here it
           exists on the very first parse, before any of those scripts.

        See .particles-load-scrim / .is-revealed in main.css for the
        gradient, the 150vh height and the slide-up reveal. --}}
  {{#is "index"}}
    <div id="particles-load-scrim" class="particles-load-scrim"></div>
  {{/is}}

  <!-- SVG refraction filter for the .glass-liquid module (assets/css/
       glass-liquid.css) — dormant until <html> also carries the
       glass-distort class (not added anywhere yet; opt in per-page/
       site when ready to test the distorted variant). Zero visual/
       paint cost while unused: a filter def with no element
       referencing it renders nothing. position:absolute + 0×0 keeps
       it out of layout without display:none, which some browsers
       treat as "don't render referenced filters either." -->
  <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" style="position:absolute; width:0; height:0; overflow:hidden;">
    <defs>
      <filter id="glass-distortion" x="0%" y="0%" width="100%" height="100%" filterUnits="objectBoundingBox">
        <feTurbulence type="fractalNoise" baseFrequency="0.004 0.009" numOctaves="1" seed="17" result="turbulence"></feTurbulence>
        <feComponentTransfer in="turbulence" result="mapped">
          <feFuncR type="gamma" amplitude="1" exponent="10" offset="0.5"></feFuncR>
          <feFuncG type="gamma" amplitude="0" exponent="1" offset="0"></feFuncG>
          <feFuncB type="gamma" amplitude="0" exponent="1" offset="0.5"></feFuncB>
        </feComponentTransfer>
        <feGaussianBlur in="turbulence" stdDeviation="3" result="softMap"></feGaussianBlur>
        <feSpecularLighting in="softMap" surfaceScale="5" specularConstant="1" specularExponent="100" lighting-color="white" result="specLight">
          <fePointLight x="-200" y="-200" z="300"></fePointLight>
        </feSpecularLighting>
        <feComposite in="specLight" operator="in" in2="SourceGraphic" result="specCut"></feComposite>
        <feDisplacementMap in="SourceGraphic" in2="softMap" scale="120" xChannelSelector="R" yChannelSelector="G" result="displaced"></feDisplacementMap>
        <feComposite in="displaced" in2="specCut" operator="over"></feComposite>
      </filter>
    </defs>
  </svg>

